WEBVTT

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.920
<i>Otome</i>:

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.840
A maiden, sweet-smelling as a flower,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:19.060
a single bud blooming in a tranquil
garden, pure and dignified.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.230
Too shy to even speak of love or romance,

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:28.520
she dares not allow herself
to dream of a kiss.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:32.900
Even so, she blooms again today--

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.990
seeking, ever seeking
happiness beyond the stars.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:52.590
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:02.080
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:07.040
"Episode 4"
"Happiness Is Under the Moonlight"

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.170
I've read all the books
I'd brought with me.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.050
"General Mathematics"

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.050
A textbook...

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:27.640
As a member of the notorious Shima family,

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.850
my classmates kept their distance.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:34.400
But I certainly didn't hate
the lessons themselves.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.070
Still...

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:37.990
that's all in the past now, too.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:51.790
Well? What do you think?

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:54.250
My! Absolutely stunning!

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:56.130
You look just like Kotori-<i>chan</i>!

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.210
Now you try, Yuzu!

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:00.630
Oh, n-no, I couldn't...

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:03.930
It's all right. I'll tie it up for you.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.810
See? This is what happens.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.030
But the fluffiness is adorable, too!

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:22.070
It's so soft and bouncy--
and shiny and healthy, too!

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:24.870
--Uh... sure is lively in here.
--I could touch it all day long!

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.660
--This must be Kotori Shira--
--I could touch it all day long!

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.080
--This must be Kotori Shira--
--Tamahiko!

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.330
It is a <i>crime </i>to peek into
a maiden's room! A <i>crime</i>!

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:35.290
S-Sorry! I'm sorry, truly!

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.420
I'd better get started on the housework.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.570
So hot...

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:07.990
Hard at work, I see.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:15.670
It's been more than half a year since
Yuzuki and I started living together.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:20.050
I want to be at your side to see all
the different Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>s.

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.510
I want to love you.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.840
That's what I think.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:27.510
I know that's what she said,

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:28.890
but I wonder...

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:34.020
It's not like I <i>want </i>her
to like me. Not at all!

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:39.520
I'll bring you some cold barley tea.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.280
A-Are you all right?

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.830
I'm sorry... I got a little
dizzy when I stood up.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:53.080
What have I done?!

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.630
Don't force yourself.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:03.970
I don't... I don't mind this,
if you're okay with it.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.470
But your right hand...

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:10.140
I can support <i>you</i>, at least.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.680
Thank you.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.100
Just for a little while, then.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:21.690
I am a pillar... I am a pillar...
I am a pillar... I am a pillar...

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:29.990
I'm all better now, thanks to you.

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:32.120
Let me just get that barley tea.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:37.040
But is she <i>really </i>okay?

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:40.880
Yuzu?

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.210
Yuzu!

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:44.710
Hang in there!

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.970
What do I do?

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:52.930
Why all the racket, brothe--

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:54.350
Yuzu?!

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:56.350
Tamako!

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.060
Stay with us, sis!

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:02.980
She's burning up.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:10.120
We have to get her to bed.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.160
I-I'll carry her!

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.490
No, thank you!

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:16.330
What, with one hand?
And what if you drop her?

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.420
Set her up in my room--it's closer.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.000
My futon's still out, too.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:28.380
And is your futon clean?

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:30.840
Yuzu cleans it every day.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:36.020
Her obi belt is in the way.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.890
Let's slip off her kimono, at least.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:39.810
Oh, right.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:42.560
"Oh, right," nothing!
Turn around this instant!

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.520
Right!

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:47.240
There we go.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:52.200
Smells like... Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.030
Sis! Yuzu!

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:55.450
Yuzu!

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:59.960
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>... Tamako-<i>san</i>...

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:05.380
There's dumpling soup
on the fire for lunch...

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:10.220
I put in lots of...
wild herbs and... veggies...

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:14.140
You like it, too... right, Tamako-<i>san</i>?

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:16.180
Yuzu...

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:19.600
--The pickles... I hate to ask,
--How can she be going on
about lunch in this condition?

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.350
--but could you... slice them?
--How can she be going on
about lunch in this condition?

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:27.400
I'll head down to the village
and bring back a doctor.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:28.740
Eh?

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.860
Do you know where I could find one?

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:35.120
I-I'm afraid I'm... not really sure.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.370
I'll have to go see.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:41.210
Wh-What about me?

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:44.790
Cool Yuzu's forehead.

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.920
You <i>can </i>do that much, can't you?

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:54.760
I believe Tamako considers things
from a rational point of view.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:58.520
She knows I'd have
trouble finding a doctor,

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:02.100
since I don't do well with strangers.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:05.270
But at least I can support Yuzu!

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:33.090
Please come in.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:39.010
She's in here.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:47.610
What are you doing?

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:52.150
I-I kept trying to bring it in, but...

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.750
Never mind. I'll do it.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.180
May she get well soon.

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:18.010
Yes, Doctor. Thank you.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:21.890
Oh, um...

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:26.770
Thank you very much for...
coming out... today.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:28.360
Here!

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:30.320
For the consult--and the medicine.

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:36.570
It's true what they say: Shima folks have
big frames and attitudes to match.

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:40.330
Why, they even look down
on the people they're <i>paying</i>.

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:44.950
That girl is overworked.

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:51.840
All this exhaustion had built up
when the heat finally did her in.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:56.590
You must've been running her
ragged from morning till night.

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:59.050
Servants are people, too!

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:00.890
"Servants"?

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:02.680
--Yuzu's--
--That girl...

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:04.600
...was bought, was she not?

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:11.360
Poor thing--ripped from her
family as payment for a debt.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:15.240
Then to live deep in the
mountains with a <i>man</i>--alone.

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:20.620
People are talking
about your little sister,

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:23.910
treating everyone like
a Shima family servant--

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:27.460
mistakenly thinking that all
she has to do is pay them.

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:31.170
No matter how rich you are,
some things cannot be fixed!

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:32.920
Like that right hand of yours.

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:39.050
Make <i>especially </i>certain this does not
go past the point of no return.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:42.140
Oh, Doctor--are you still here?

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.390
Let me show you out.

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:54.150
Tamako...

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:58.070
Members of the Shima family
just happen to be taller, that's all.

00:10:58.070 --> 00:10:59.570
Mmm.

00:10:59.570 --> 00:11:05.080
I was struggling at the station when
some villagers offered to take me here.

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:07.120
I <i>did </i>thank them.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:08.410
Mmm.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:11.210
Yuzu is no servant,

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:14.710
and there's nothing shameful between you.

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:15.710
That's right.

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:20.260
If you knew all this,
why didn't you <i>say </i>anything?!

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:23.510
Brother?

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:28.020
Yuzu, overworked...
what a cruel thing I've done.

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:30.690
It's all my fault.

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:36.440
It's mine--for barging in out of nowhere.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:39.820
I'll go look after her.

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:43.070
Tamako!

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:47.040
Take good care of Yuzu.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.330
I don't need <i>you </i>to tell me that!

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:56.840
Luckily, Tamako happened
to be around today.

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:58.880
Had she not been here...

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:06.470
Poor young Yuzu: sold to
my father, torn from her family.

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:10.480
Someone as good as her
<i>must </i>find happiness.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:13.560
But if she stays with me...

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:26.410
One day, we'll be past
the point of no return.

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:30.580
Like that right hand of yours.

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:43.430
Oh, Yuzu! Tamako's here to wipe
you down, so let's get changed!

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:45.510
Wait, what?

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:50.220
Oh! I'm sorry. I've already changed.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:53.270
What?! When did <i>this </i>happen?

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:56.350
Come on, you can't be overdoing things!

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:58.770
I'm fine!

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.980
But how's Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:04.820
I haven't seen him--how's he getting on?

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:08.320
Has he eaten dinner?
Taken a bath--brushed his teeth?

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:09.620
Yuzu...

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:14.910
Are you <i>really </i>happy with
that brother of mine?

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:16.620
Huh?

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:20.130
He's entirely useless in times like this.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:22.710
You ought to marry someone better.

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:27.550
But if I do that, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>
will wind up all alone again!

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:37.190
Long ago, one of my friends was
being mistreated by her mother.

00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:40.150
She'd always say
"I wish I were dead already"

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:44.190
and "I'm so unhappy--
I should just disappear."

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:46.450
Like Tamahiko...

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:51.280
I wanted to help this girl,
so I asked my mother.

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:55.870
How can I cheer her up, Momma?

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:59.170
Once someone's heart has
withdrawn into a shell, Yuzu,

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:02.130
it's not that easy to change.

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:07.840
That girl's heart is hers alone.

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:09.640
That can't be right!

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:13.810
I just have to cheer her up--I <i>have </i>to!

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:15.810
In that case...

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:20.190
Watch over her,
believing that the time will come

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:25.190
when, after all sorts of
experiences and lots of thinking,

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.570
she'll turn toward happiness on her own.

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:31.620
With a reassuring friend in her corner,

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:35.160
the day will come when
she'll think it's okay to change.

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:37.290
No matter how much time it takes,

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:42.670
you alone must keep believing,
stay by her side, and watch over her.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:47.550
And so I believe.

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:51.430
I believe that one day,
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>, too,

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:53.390
will entertain the thought of happiness.

00:14:55.930 --> 00:15:02.020
You really do think about
Tamahiko a lot, don't you.

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:06.780
After all, he <i>is </i>going to be
my husband one day.

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:13.070
"Husband"? Wh-What am I saying?!

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:16.870
Your fever's spiking again, Yuzu!

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:30.510
When I think I'd like to
do something for him,

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:32.640
my body moves on its own.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:38.600
My body... moved on its own...

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:49.570
Is Yuzu all right?

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.990
You don't have to do anything, brother.

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:09.840
How are you feeling, Yuzu?

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:19.680
Yuzu!

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:30.440
Blood?!

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:34.530
Can't... breathe...

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:38.580
What's this?

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:44.500
My breathing... Tamako-<i>san</i>... please...

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:47.710
Take this... off...

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:52.130
So you skinned your hand tearing
the bandage, trying to take it off.

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:54.050
Good thing you weren't coughing up blood.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:56.850
Please... take it off...

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:58.100
Huh?!

00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:01.100
T-Tamako! Tamako, where are you?

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:09.690
Guess I'll have to...

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:16.910
What the--it's so tight,
it's squeezing her ribs!

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:19.080
No wonder you can't breathe!

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:27.210
Forgive me, Yuzu.

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:33.880
I'm saving a life... I'm saving a life...

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:53.690
I can breathe... much better...

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:55.780
Tamako-<i>sa</i>--

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:57.200
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:17:57.200 --> 00:18:00.740
I'm so sorry you had to see
such a disgraceful sight!

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:07.330
My big chest has always been a problem.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:08.790
In my girls' school days,

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:12.300
I was so embarrassed that
I wore a bandage to hide them.

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:17.220
Could this be the second
of her two worries?

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:20.100
I mean, I don't get taller,
but <i>these </i>get bigger--

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:23.350
like they're absorbing all
of my body's nutrition!

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:26.350
They're wrong for a kimono,
I look fat, my shoulders ache,

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:28.480
and the bandages are stifling!

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:30.270
I'm sorry!

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:35.690
I'm the worst possible man for you.

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:39.280
I make you sick and then
can't even care for you properly.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:41.990
When I finally think I'm helping,

00:18:41.990 --> 00:18:44.870
I wind up embarrassing you.

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:47.910
Everything just backfires.

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:48.920
I...

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:53.840
I can support <i>you</i>, at least.

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:58.380
I can't even support you.

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:04.430
Before I do something to you
that I can never take back,

00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:07.430
it might be best to break
off this relationship.

00:19:08.980 --> 00:19:11.810
I can get by on my own.

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:15.480
I'll tell my father.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:17.400
You go on home.

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:22.320
It was only a short time... but thank you.

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:26.120
I want... I want...

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.870
I want you to be happ--

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:33.710
I'm not leaving.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:41.010
I'll be by your side, no matter what.

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:45.930
And me? I'll be fine.

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:49.060
I'm not that much of a wimpy little girl.

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:56.980
Yuzu is... strong.

00:19:56.980 --> 00:19:59.400
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:02.910
Far, <i>far </i>stronger than I think.

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:09.660
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:11.290
It's morning!

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:15.000
Did you sleep well?

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.840
Yuzu! You're up and about?!

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:20.590
Yes! I'm good as new.

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:23.260
I always did have a hardy constitution.

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:27.680
No way! Rest another day--
just to be on the safe side!

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:32.600
Thank you, but I really am just fine.

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:35.560
Now: do you smell that?

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:40.690
<i>Hittsumi</i>!

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:42.320
That's correct!

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:46.570
And Tamako-<i>san </i>made us rice balls.

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:50.370
Hurry up, now,

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:51.710
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:55.330
In that moment,

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:58.000
my heart was caught in a squeezing grip,

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:00.630
and something shot
bubbling up to my brain:

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:04.970
I want to make Yuzu happy.

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:09.060
I...

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:11.310
I want to be the man who can do that.

00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:21.820
Whatever made me think that, anyway?

00:21:23.280 --> 00:21:28.070
I mean, <i>me</i>? How presumptuous can I get?

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:32.000
Lately, I'm prone to forgetting
that I'm a pessimist.

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:35.710
I've really got to remind myself again.

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:40.050
Pessimist pessimist
pessimist pessimist pessimist...

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:46.680
Sister Yuzu, brother Tamahiko,
I have something to tell you.

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:50.640
Why so formal, Tamako?

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:54.180
I shall be returning home tomorrow.

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:55.190
Huh?!

00:21:56.850 --> 00:22:00.270
I'm thinking of becoming a doctor.

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:03.530
What?!

00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:45.130
Tamako-<i>san </i>is as precious
to me as a real little sister.

00:23:45.130 --> 00:23:50.260
I want to support her at all times,
from the bottom of my heart!
